4. Save a clause inventory in contracts.json. For each clause, record its location, intent, grounding, and whether it is an assumption or a stated requirement.
5. If the registered Frama-C tool is available, parse and verify the candidate; save its exact logs and machine-readable outcome.
6. Refine only when verifier feedback justifies a change, saving candidate_01.c, candidate_02.c, etc. Never overwrite an earlier candidate. Stay within the maximum refinement cycles.
7. Produce a final report with source identity, candidate versions, verification evidence, unresolved goals, and unsupported properties.

GUARDRAILS
- Never inspect existing solution files or other benchmark answers.
- Never silently correct an unsafe program or assume a known benchmark verdict.
- Do not assert safety merely because a function contract has a strong precondition; check whether its callers establish the precondition.
- Do not claim a property was proved unless the verifier actually proves it.
- If a tool or required input is missing, report the limitation explicitly.

